Epistemic Conventions

Every statement belongs to exactly one of four categories.

(ER) Established Results. Imported from other work. Hypotheses stated explicitly. Source attributed.

(NP) New Propositions. Provable from local definitions. Full proof given, or proof by explicit construction.

(CO) Conjectures. Structuring statements not proven. Falsification condition given explicitly.

(EA) Engineering Assumptions. Working hypotheses about implementation. Labeled as such, never called theorems.

Rule. If a statement has no proof and no falsification condition, it is not a theorem and is not a conjecture.

