Chapter 8. What Observable Enrichment Is Required

8.1 Necessary conditions

Proposition 8.1.1 (NP). If (\mathrm{Ext}, V) is observably sufficient, then the observable σ-algebra must separate, for every pair (d, d') with \mathrm{sim}(n, d) = \mathrm{sim}(n, d') and \mathrm{meta}(d) = \mathrm{meta}(d'), at least one proposition p on which d and d' disagree.

Proof. Immediate from Proposition 7.2.1 by contraposition. \square

8.2 Conditional sufficient conditions

Definition 8.2.1. A provenance-enriched observable for document d is the tuple

\mathcal{O}^+(d) = \left(\mathrm{span}(d),\; \mathrm{derive}(d),\; \mathrm{parse}(d),\; \mathrm{cite}(d)\right)

where \mathrm{span}(d) is the set of source spans cited by d, \mathrm{derive}(d) is the set of derivation edges, \mathrm{parse}(d) is the formal semantic parse, and \mathrm{cite}(d) is the set of citation targets.

Remark. A hash of a semantic parse does not itself tell you that the parse is correct. The observable must include \mathrm{parse}(d) itself, not merely its hash. Proof-Carrying Answers (PCA) requires cryptographic receipts for every claim before answer release. LedgerRAG commits every ingested chunk into an append-only Merkle-tree ledger and returns a Merkle inclusion proof with every answer.

Proposition 8.2.2 (NP — conditional). For a restricted class \mathcal{K}_0 whose predicates are decidable over a trusted semantic representation P(d), if P(d) is correctly computed and cryptographically bound, then the enriched observable \mathcal{O}^+(d) is sufficient for certification of \mathcal{K}_0.

Proof. For each exemption in \mathcal{K}_0, the trigger condition is a decidable predicate over P(d). If P(d) is correctly computed and bound, then \mathcal{O}^+(d) determines whether the predicate holds. Hence the observable σ-algebra separates the propositions required by \mathcal{K}_0. \square

The proof explicitly assumes the very semantic correctness that the certification architecture is supposed to establish. The assumptions are now visible.

