Chapter 16. Error Taxonomy

16.1 The full state vector

Define the full state vector:

\boxed{
X = (C, E, L, D) \in \{0,1\}^4
}

where C = coverage, E = evidence validity, L = legal validity, D = disclosure violation.

The five named classes are equivalence classes of the 16 possible states:

Type Condition Interpretation
I C=0 Information not found
II C=1, E=0 Right documents, unsupported claim
III C=1, E=1, L=0 Correct evidence, wrong law
IV C=1, E=1, L=1, D=0 Valid chain
