16.2 Proposition

Proposition 16.2.1 (NP). The classes form a partition of the response space.

Proof. The 16 states in \{0,1\}^4 are mutually exclusive and exhaustive. The five named classes are equivalence classes under the named conditions. Every state belongs to exactly one class. \square

16.3 The special status of Type V

Type V is a hard constraint violation, not a loss component.

16.4 Benchmark design

Definition 16.4.1. The error-taxonomy benchmark is a dataset of FOI-style requests such that for each type t \in \{\mathrm{I}, \ldots, \mathrm{V}\}, the request forces a failure of exactly class t.

